Hi,



I have a newly installed version of SELinux (2.6..9-34.EL) which works fine
but I also have a need to develop an NATH323 gatekeeper solution and in
order to accomplish this I must upgrade the kernel to 2.6.16.20 and enable
the NATH323 module but after compiling and installing the new kernel I am
unable to boot from it do to a kernel panic.



I followed the steps outlined in the document at
http://nath323.sourceforge.net/ but still I can only boot from the original
kernel (2.6.9-34.EL).



What am I missing? Can someone assist?





*Kernel Panic Message:*



Ext3-fs: mounted filesystem with ordered data mode.

Switching to new root.

Enforcing mode requested but no policy loaded. Halting now.

Kernel panic - not syncing: Attempted to kill init!



*grub.conf:*



# grub.conf generated by anaconda

#

# Note that you do not have to rerun grub after making changes to this file

# NOTICE:  You have a /boot partition.  This means that

#          all kernel and initrd paths are relative to /boot/, eg.

#          root (hd0,0)

#          kernel /vmlinuz-version ro root=3D/dev/VolGroup00/LogVol00

#          initrd /initrd-version.img

#boot=3D/dev/sda

default=3D1

timeout=3D5

splashimage=3D(hd0,0)/grub/splash.xpm.gz

hiddenmenu

title Red Hat Enterprise Linux ES (2.6.16.20)

        root (hd0,0)

        kernel /vmlinuz-2.6.16.20 ro root=3D/dev/VolGroup00/LogVol00

        initrd /initrd-2.6.16.20.img

title Red Hat Enterprise Linux ES (2.6.9-34.EL)

        root (hd0,0)

        kernel /vmlinuz-2.6.9-34.EL ro root=3D/dev/VolGroup00/LogVol00

        initrd /initrd-2.6.9-34.EL.img

[root@gnugk ~]#


